WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.030
A ship at sea, with
500 merchants on board.

2
00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:07.950
The captain learns that one
man plans to kill them all.

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.680
In a Buddhist story, the captain
is the Buddha-to-be in a past life.

4
00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:15.480
He kills the robber, out of compassion.

5
00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:17.960
Yet many Buddhists keep the first precept,

6
00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:21.210
against killing, as
close to exceptionless.

7
00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:24.900
So which is it: rules, results, character,

8
00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:26.870
or something else entirely?

9
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:30.190
In this mission, you'll set
Buddhist teaching beside Kant,

10
00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:33.470
Bentham and Aristotle, column by column.

11
00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:37.800
Then you'll place four scholars' readings
of Buddhist ethics on a spectrum.

12
00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:41.620
Your mission: find out whether
Buddhist ethics is about rules,

13
00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:44.510
results, character, or something else.
